{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science","id":30352,"title":"\"I roll Appearance+Science too blind him with Science!\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-15T02:56:26-08:00","id":30352,"title":"\"I roll Appearance+Science too blind him with Science!\"","content":"So this question keeps popping up in my head as I gloss over the combinations of Attribute and Ability there could be. Of them, I have concluded that Appearance and anything that isn't some physical act of some form like dancing or something doesn't make too much sense to me. Appearance and Academics, what are you doing here? Making yourself look pretty with your college degree? Is the occult making yourself a sexy zombie? Technology a Transformer or something? This is really baffling me. Intelligence+Anything at first seems stupid as well, but at the very least it makes sense when it becomes the knowledge check. Intelligence+Brawl, &quot;His kungfu is strong!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Can somebody clarify to me what one would even be rolling with something like &quot;Manipulation+Awereness/Alertness&quot;, &quot;Appearance+(Anything Really)&quot;, or even any Physical with anything else? &quot;Strength+Finance&quot; would be what? Me punching a guy with money?<br /> <br /> Excuse the sarcasm or whatever tone I am having. TIred, no sleep. And this question is racking my mind like crazy. It's like this system could theoretically allow for about 270 or so different combinations of rolls, but then there are things that wouldn't make sense together. So is it technically not logical or am I just not expanding my thought process and imagination here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1490-akasen","name":"Akasen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T04:03:25-08:00","id":30365,"title":"","content":"I don't quite see why you assume that every Ability should be rolled with every Attribute and make sense. The fact that the number of combinations theoretically is 270 (and that's before messing with secondaries) does not automatically mean that each of those combinations actually corresponds with an action requiring a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T08:35:47-08:00","id":30436,"title":"","content":"While I'm with HOD on this, I think there is a slight issue with the cWOD Attribute line up. Or at least as it gets defined in the books (some of the other books use the same spread but manage to redefine things a bit to make more combinations make more sense).<br /> <br /> Appearance, for example, is heavily under utilized in the game and the main mechanic it sees (first impressions) is often punishingly stupid and gets ignored. This is mostly because the cWOD generally treats App as a pretty passive thing outside of seduction. In other ST games, it is used more actively as the default for basing your action on non-verbal displays or body-language. So you could roll App + Intimidation to look really scary (even if you aren't) where Manipulation would require having to convince them that you're threatening with words. App + Academics would imply knowing how to look the part and get people to take you serious as someone that probably knows what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> Some of the later games also try to ax the &quot;Attribute : Ability&quot; analogs like Perception vs. Alertness. This seems to help considerably in terms of cutting down on pairings that don't seem to have any practical applications.<br /> <br /> Even so, there are always going to be pairings that are either non-functional or exceedingly niche in application to be useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T13:36:56-08:00","id":30559,"title":"","content":"First Impression Capacity + Hypothesis Testing = making sure that your professor knows your name for the right reasons, <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r6AymaTvfXE\" target=\"_blank\">explaining difficult concepts to little children so that they pay attention and ask questions, even if they don't get it.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T21:36:37-08:00","id":30764,"title":"","content":"Appearance + Science: Kelly LeBrock circa 1985?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T04:24:30-08:00","id":30894,"title":"","content":"I had a fellow player ask if they can roll Appearance + Firearms so his character could look good with a gun. ST called him a dumbass and said he wasn't supposed to use those traits like that. So he thought a moment then asked if he could roll Charisma + Firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:00:41-08:00","id":31106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=30894#post30894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a fellow player ask if they can roll Appearance + Firearms so his character could look good with a gun. ST called him a dumbass and said he wasn't supposed to use those traits like that. So he thought a moment then asked if he could roll Charisma + Firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly from a players perspective I could see that they would want to be looking cool while using their firearms, but there doesn't need to be a roll with it. I would just say if you have such in such in manip/cha/app (st choice) then sure you look cool while doing it. The reason why he/she was called a dumbass, is because it's minutia and slows down actual storytelling, or a fight. Sure you can waste some of your dice by doing a cool matrix flip kick up a wall and as you come back down shoot someone in the head...and add like +4 to the dc (2 for the two actions, and 2 for the called shot) or...you could just shoot the dude in the head. Cinematics can be left up to your own imagination, and there's nothing game worthy for &quot;style&quot; points.<br /> <br /> ~edit just an after thought, if doing so to prove something to someone, then I def would allow it, but it shouldn't come up often enough to warrant it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","user":"Asssassin","date":". 12-16-2013, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:24:19-08:00","id":31114,"title":"","content":"Whether or not it is minutiae or not is situational. Maybe looking cool was important to the story. More important than murdering someone with an optimal shot.<br /> <br /> The &quot;there doesn't need to be a roll with it&quot; could be said of any action. You don't need to roll to shoot someone if it would slow things down and the ST feels you should be allowed to execute the bastard and move on.<br /> <br /> Style points might not count in combat, but who said it was a combat situation? Style points definitely count for social focused efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:28:53-08:00","id":31120,"title":"","content":"Appearance + [any social ability like Subterfuge, Intimidation, Leadership, Animal Ken] makes a good deal of sense and tends to come up. Personally, I like the Appearance + Firearms idea, and would happily let a player roll that.<br /> <br /> Intelligence + Anything can be a figuring stuff out roll. For example, a Sabbat pack (PCs) was torturing an enemy captive for everything he knew about the Camarilla in the neighboring city. They had to roll Intelligence + Politics figure out the meaning behind what they learned, and understand the implications of messing with some of the named people. Failing the roll meant &quot;You have a list of names and descriptions&quot;. Success let them figure out that the position of Brujah Primogen was in contension right now, know the who Prince's favorite is, and have an idea of the factions involved.<br /> <br /> Even though some trait combinations make little sense or are extremely esoteric, the flexibility and potential of the Storyteller system is still nice. The common rolls make sense. When the common roll don't apply, we've got lots to work with to find a roll that does. Some of the less common rolls that have happened in my games:<br /> <br /> Appearance + Melee when trying to show off with butterfly knives, and winning serious respect for doing it well<br /> <br /> Strength + Etiquette to help a lady climb through a window gracefully, without looking up her skirts or mishandling her<br /> <br /> Charisma + Occult to make a good impression on a blood sorcerer by showing how well you've studied. This earned someone a shot at apprenticeship.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T12:54:22-08:00","id":31138,"title":"","content":"I always liked the Scion example of letting a bookish character use Strength + Academics when carrying a backpack full of books instead of Strength + Athletics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T13:05:49-08:00","id":31149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=31114#post31114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not it is minutiae or not is situational. Maybe looking cool was important to the story. More important than murdering someone with an optimal shot.<br /> <br /> The &quot;there doesn't need to be a roll with it&quot; could be said of any action. You don't need to roll to shoot someone if it would slow things down and the ST feels you should be allowed to execute the bastard and move on.<br /> <br /> Style points might not count in combat, but who said it was a combat situation? Style points definitely count for social focused efforts.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's why I put my edit in...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T13:18:37-08:00","id":31162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=31138#post31138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked the Scion example of letting a bookish character use Strength + Academics when carrying a backpack full of books instead of Strength + Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works better in WoD than in a derivation of Aeonverse, which separated out endurance and power to different Abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T13:23:10-08:00","id":31171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=30894#post30894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a fellow player ask if they can roll Appearance + Firearms so his character could look good with a gun. ST called him a dumbass and said he wasn't supposed to use those traits like that. So he thought a moment then asked if he could roll Charisma + Firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have given that the OK maybe. I dunno. He is trying to look good with a gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1490-akasen","name":"Akasen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T02:45:10-08:00","id":31561,"title":"","content":"To clarify the Player wasn't trying to make his character look good while shooting someone. He wanted to have his character look good while carrying a weapon in the open. The ST in saying he wasn't supposed to use the traits that way wasn't telling him he couldn't make that roll, he was trying to point out the effect he was going for wasn't important to the story, but the player missed that point and thought the ST was telling him he was using the wrong trait combo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  fixed typos 12-17-2013, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T04:56:10-08:00","id":31588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asssassin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=31106#post31106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly from a players perspective I could see that they would want to be looking cool while using their firearms, but there doesn't need to be a roll with it. I would just say if you have such in such in manip/cha/app (st choice) then sure you look cool while doing it. The reason why he/she was called a dumbass, is because it's minutia and slows down actual storytelling, or a fight. Sure you can waste some of your dice by doing a cool matrix flip kick up a wall and as you come back down shoot someone in the head...and add like +4 to the dc (2 for the two actions, and 2 for the called shot) or...you could just shoot the dude in the head. Cinematics can be left up to your own imagination, and there's nothing game worthy for &quot;style&quot; points.<br /> <br /> ~edit just an after thought, if doing so to prove something to someone, then I def would allow it, but it shouldn't come up often enough to warrant it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should always be allowed, under the Rule of Cool <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Obviously group-specific, but hey, anything that makes a person feel connected to their character and awesome, sounds like a winner to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T09:57:55-08:00","id":31740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=31561#post31561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify the Player wasn't trying to make his character look good while shooting someone. He wanted to have his character look good while carrying a weapon in the open. The ST in saying he wasn't supposed to use the traits that way wasn't telling him he couldn't make that roll, he was trying to point out the effect he was going for wasn't important to the story, but the player missed that point and thought the ST was telling him he was using the wrong trait combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy didn't attack a gazebo, too, did he? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T12:38:38-08:00","id":31834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=31561#post31561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify the Player wasn't trying to make his character look good while shooting someone. He wanted to have his character look good while carrying a weapon in the open. The ST in saying he wasn't supposed to use the traits that way wasn't telling him he couldn't make that roll, he was trying to point out the effect he was going for wasn't important to the story, but the player missed that point and thought the ST was telling him he was using the wrong trait combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup that's pretty much what I figured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T03:44:08-08:00","id":34878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/30352-i-roll-appearance-science-too-blind-him-with-science?p=31740#post31740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This guy didn't attack a gazebo, too, did he? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hehehe I think if his character hadn't gotten run over by a truck in a spectacularly botched Leaping from semi to semi.... (&quot;Are you SURE you want to jump from the top of the parallel semi to the wind shield of the next one, when you only have 2 dots in Dex and 1 in Athletics at Freeway speeds?&quot;) yeah.... the ST might have thrown out the gazebo just to mess with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T09:29:12-07:00","id":260674,"title":"","content":"This reminded me of a time when the group, all male characters, went to a brothel and asked the ST to roll Dexterity + Linguistics to perform great cunilingus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T00:41:45-07:00","id":263508,"title":"","content":"I guess first you must concrete what exactly you want to do with your ability.<br /> For example Melee:<br /> 1. Strike an enemy : Dexterity/Strength + Melee, maybe Wits.<br /> Logically you can use your dexterity or wits striking with Dagger, but not with a Greatsword.<br /> 2. Dagger-play - Dexterity+Performance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3926-duvall","name":"DuVall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T00:46:54-07:00","id":263510,"title":"","content":"For example Queen of the Damned from &quot;Till Dusk to Dawn&quot;<br /> Her sexual dance with a python may be rolled with an Appereance+Animal Ken instead of Appereance+Performance(dance), empowered with Awe and Feral Whispers or Tongue of the Asp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3926,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3926-duvall","user":"DuVall","date":". 09-23-2014, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3926-duvall","name":"DuVall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T19:24:10-07:00","id":265896,"title":"","content":"Im puzzled with Appearance attribute to. First, i never use it when make my characters. Second, when i run games my players never take this attribute for they characters, even girls go for charisma instead (despite my expectations). Feels like this attribute doubles Charisma and provides little use. I even planed do my house rules and edit character sheet putting instead some social background style trait like Influence or Status. Nosferatu Appearance 0 then would be as forced Flaw and if player wish it could take Merit &quot;Beautiful&quot; or somenting like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2148-lachplesis","name":"Lachplesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T20:50:45-07:00","id":265933,"title":"","content":"As I mentioned up thread, Appearance doesn't have to go as much as the rather narrow definition of &quot;low App = ugly, high App = beautiful,&quot; nature of how it is treated.<br /> <br /> If you redefine it to be how well you use your body to social ends, whatever body type you happen to have, it becomes a much easier thing to deal with. This cuts a bit off of Charisma, but it creates a trait you want to have for lots of concepts beyond just looking good. You can be so ugly that Nosferatu vomit when they see you, and with the redefined App 5 throw that around like a weapon to disgust, intimidate, and demoralize anything that thinks of being in the same room as you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T21:31:20-07:00","id":267187,"title":"","content":"It's not a hard rule, since we don't generally use that First Impression rule and tend to RP social actions with your attributes affecting how you are listened or sometimes rolled after you have said what you set out to say to see how well your character spoke it but Appearance is extremely important to have at the least in the average range and useful to have over average. Why? Because otherwise people wont give you the time a day, they simply tend to ignore you or even avoid you, instead of actually listening which means your huge manipulation pool, or Charisma pool, are useless as people rarely take the necessary time to listen to you enough to find out you are such a swell guy.<br /> <br /> For example.<br /> <br /> In my last Vampire game the players met a Nosferatu who was rather sociable, but despite having high Obfuscate didn't really bother hiding his appearance in Vampiric company. Circumstances were such that they were more or less forced to be and work together which is why the players were more or less forced to listen to him. Still thanks to his appearance they had this disgust that was rather hard to get over that is to say for the first few whole conversations they shied away from him and just tried to get him to leave or shut up solely because of his appearance, but as they had little choice over the matter he got the time to sway them over with his words, wit and most of all natural Charisma. Still it was a struggle to get to use that Charisma in a manner that would matter since the people had little to none amounting interest in actually knowing him.<br /> <br /> Where as in another game, Aberrant to be exact, there was a player who not only had high appearance, she was a model, but actual Mega-Appearance to boot and she was blunt, to the point rude, and treated people like trash still those people were all willing to take it from her and wanted to listen in on her every word. Why? To be close to her and to give her the impression they cared so as to get closer to her. That is the power of Appearance it is often Passive in that you do not necessarily need to actively use it (though dancing, making an entrance and seduction are all possible active use examples) but it still affects everyone who can see you and can make it very hard to be heard or noticed or alternatively make it very hard not to be noticed.<br /> <br /> As for my own character I tend to take 3+ Appearance for most of my characters unless my concept involves them looking completely average or even ugly. Because who wouldn't want to look good when given the choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T16:36:01-07:00","id":273315,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting question, and all interesting opinions.<br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind: to a quick survey of any people, anytime anywhere. I'm pretty sure you'll find that if they could \u201cmagically\u201d improve something, Appearance would be a first choice for an overwhelming majority. It has a huge impact on social interactions and even your whole quality of life, even when there's no sexual or romantic interaction (at least officially). Look objectively on how you react to the little everyday things when it's toward a truly beautiful and charming man or woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Playing on <a href=\"https://tousrolistes.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">French Online virtual tabletop rpg community</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3723-blacky","name":"Blacky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3723_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T17:34:29-07:00","id":273339,"title":"","content":"Manipulation + Fire Arms = Manipulate someone so they can give you all their money or else you will blow their head off..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T18:27:54-07:00","id":275925,"title":"","content":"I could see Appearance + Science for a character who has their own science-based tv show. Charisma is important too, but a good enough roll with Appearance could make many viewers forget you are obviously reading from cue cards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}